From 39e3b5452ee425a4c32edbb110bca0903aa119a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178 <19559105+ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:56:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix audit_census compliance, -0.0 select codegen,
 packed/bitfield layout, ld -r symtab, and #error expansion

- Restore audit_census compliance after PR #877, #880, and #881:
  * Extract try_fuse_copy_bridged_load in src/backend/x86/codegen/peephole/passes/load_op_fuse.rs so fuse_load_into_alu stays under 300 lines (fns_over_300: 231).
  * Trim verbose inline comments in eliminate_redundant_zero_extend (src/backend/x86/codegen/peephole/passes/redundant_ext.rs) so fns_over_500 stays at 93.
  * Document CCC_VOLATILE_REDUCE_LANES, CCC_VOLATILE_REDUCE_BUDGET, and CCC_PEEPHOLE_BUDGET in engineering/PERF-volatile-reduction-interleave.md and remove 3 phantom comment-only knob strings in avx.rs, pushf_elim.rs, and loop_preheader.rs (knob_literals: 510, knobs_undocumented: 283).
- CG-07r (src/backend/x86/codegen/comparison.rs): Guard select_operand_to_reg's movl $0 shortcut with IrConst::is_all_zero_bits() instead of is_zero(), preserving the sign bit of IEEE-754 -0.0f / -0.0 and non-canonical decimal zero bit patterns.
- PF-16 (src/backend/x86/codegen/comparison.rs, src/backend/x86/codegen/emit.rs, src/passes/integer_bounds.rs, src/backend/generation.rs):
  * Emit 5-byte movl into the 32-bit sub-register for F32/D32 constants and non-negative 32-bit integer immediates instead of 7-byte movq / 10-byte movabsq when bit 31 is set.
  * Extend Bounds::instruction with Add, Sub(Const, rhs), URem, UDiv, and Select, and seed collect_bitop_nonneg_values from integer_bounds::nonneg_i32_values so __builtin_ffs and 32 - __builtin_clz avoid redundant movslq %eax, %rax.
- LK-20 (src/backend/x86/linker/emit_rel.rs): Map input symbol index 0 (STN_UNDEF) to output symbol 0 and skip index 0 in the local-symbol loop during relocatable linking (ld -r).
- FE-24 (src/frontend/preprocessor/pipeline.rs): Preserve #error pp-tokens verbatim without macro expansion per C11 6.10.5p1 / C23 6.10.6p1.
- MS-12 & MS-20 (src/common/types.rs): Honor explicit aligned(N) on per-field packed members, route per-field packed bitfields through layout_packed_bitfield, and round trailing bitfields by actual bit position before struct-alignment padding.
